    "scientific_verdict": "Across nearest-neighbor, two-shell, and isotropic depolarizing modular noise kernels on Z_q, the non-zero difference visibilities {lambda_d}_{d=1}^{q-1} satisfy sum_{d=1}^{q-1} lambda_d = q * K_eta(0) - 1 and sum_{d=1}^{q-1} lambda_d^2 = q * ||K_eta||_2^2 - 1. Matched-harmonic weighting w_d^* = lambda_d achieves SNR_matched = q * ||K_eta||_2^2 - 1 and strictly outperforms uniform difference weighting whenever K_eta is non-uniform on Z_q \\ {0}, with an exact SNR gap equal to q * sum_{e=1}^{q-1} (K_eta(e) - (1 - K_eta(0))/(q - 1))^2."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact Sum of Non-Zero Harmonic Visibilities via K_eta(0)",
      "statement": "For any symmetric probability distribution K_eta on Z_q, the sum of non-zero harmonic visibilities lambda_d = sum_e K_eta(e) cos(2*pi*d*e/q) over d in {1, ..., q-1} equals q * K_eta(0) - 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Exact Parseval Collision-Purity Law for Quadratic Visibility",
      "statement": "For any symmetric probability distribution K_eta on Z_q, the sum of squared non-zero harmonic visibilities over d in {1, ..., q-1} equals q * sum_(e in Z_q) K_eta(e)^2 - 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Cauchy-Schwarz Matched-Filter Optimality and Physical-Space SNR Gap Identity",
      "statement": "Matched-harmonic weighting w_d* = lambda_d maximizes SNR(w; K_eta) at SNR_matched = q * sum_e K_eta(e)^2 - 1, exceeding uniform weighting SNR_unif = (q * K_eta(0) - 1)^2 / (q - 1) by exactly q * sum_(e=1)^(q-1) (K_eta(e) - (1 - K_eta(0))/(q - 1))^2 >= 0."
    }
  ],
  "title": "DCP Multi-Harmonic Weighted Fisher Decoder Audit: Exact Parseval Mean-Square Visibility Law, Zero-Lag Inversion Identity, and Matched-Filter Optimality"
}
